# Always install devDependencies, even when NODE_ENV=production.
#
# This API is built from source on the host (Render runs `npm ci` then `tsc`),
# and NODE_ENV must be `production` at runtime for the startup guards in
# src/env.ts. But NODE_ENV=production makes npm set `omit=dev`, which drops
# typescript and @types/* — so the build fails on every reference to `process`,
# `Buffer` and `node:crypto`.
#
# Setting this here rather than in the build command means it holds whatever
# command the platform ends up running. Render stores the build command when a
# blueprint is first applied and does not re-read render.yaml on later pushes,
# so a fix that lives only in render.yaml can silently fail to apply.
#
# The shipped container carries some build-only packages as a result. That is
# a few MB, against a build that cannot break in this way again.
include=dev
